{"slug":"/students/subjects/mathematics/number-systems/logic/","source":"students/subjects/mathematics/number-systems/logic.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Logic — Propositions & Truth Tables","description":"","subject":"mathematics","body":"<header class=\"bg-teal-700 text-white py-3 mb-6\"><div class=\"max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 flex items-center justify-between\"><div class=\"font-semibold\">Logic</div><a href=\"/students/subjects/mathematics/number-systems/\" class=\"text-white/90\">Back</a></div></header>\n\n  <main class=\"max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 space-y-6\">\n    <section class=\"card\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold\">Basic Connectives</h2><div class=\"mt-2 text-gray-700\">AND (∧), OR (∨), NOT (¬), Implication (→). Understand truth-table evaluation for compound statements.</div></section>\n\n    <section class=\"card\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold\">Truth Table — P → Q</h2>\n      <div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-gray-700\">Implication is false only when P true and Q false.</div>\n      <div class=\"mt-4 overflow-auto\">\n        <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\"><tbody><tr class=\"bg-gray-100\"><th class=\"border px-2\">P</th><th class=\"border px-2\">Q</th><th class=\"border px-2\">P → Q</th></tr><tr><td class=\"border px-2\">F</td><td class=\"border px-2\">F</td><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border px-2\">F</td><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td><td class=\"border px-2\">F</td><td class=\"border px-2\">F</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td><td class=\"border px-2\">T</td></tr></tbody></table>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"card\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold\">Practice</h2>\n      <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-3\">\n        <div class=\"p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded\"><div class=\"font-medium\">1) When is P → Q false?</div><input id=\"lo1\" class=\"mt-2 p-2 border rounded w-full\" placeholder=\"e.g., P true and Q false\"><div class=\"mt-2 flex gap-2\"><button id=\"loc1\" class=\"px-3 py-1 bg-teal-700 text-white rounded\">Check</button><button id=\"loh1\" class=\"px-3 py-1 border rounded\">Hint</button></div><div id=\"lofb1\" class=\"mt-2 text-sm\"></div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded\"><div class=\"font-medium\">2) Negate: \"All students passed the test.\"</div><input id=\"lo2\" class=\"mt-2 p-2 border rounded w-full\" placeholder=\"e.g., There exists a student who did not pass\"><div class=\"mt-2 flex gap-2\"><button id=\"loc2\" class=\"px-3 py-1 bg-teal-700 text-white rounded\">Check</button><button id=\"loh2\" class=\"px-3 py-1 border rounded\">Hint</button></div><div id=\"lofb2\" class=\"mt-2 text-sm\"></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <div class=\"text-right\"><button id=\"loQuiz\" class=\"bg-teal-700 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded\">Mini Quiz</button></div>\n  </main>\n\n  <div id=\"loModal\" class=\"hidden fixed inset-0 bg-black/40 z-40 flex items-center justify-center\"><div class=\"bg-white rounded p-6 max-w-md w-full\"><div id=\"loContent\"></div><div class=\"mt-4 text-right\"><button id=\"loClose\" class=\"px-3 py-1 border rounded\">Close</button></div></div></div>\n\n  \n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"bg-teal-50 font-sans","bodyStyle":"","css":[".card{background:#fff;padding:1rem;border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(2,6,23,0.06)} .mono{font-family:ui-monospace, monospace}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}